  "summary_en": "Philosophical paper examining ethical dilemmas of using nursing robots for autism spectrum disorder therapy. It argues robots cannot be responsible subjects or moral agents, may cause emotional deception and privacy problems, and therefore should not be fully autonomous or replace physiotherapists.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Robots cannot be subjects of responsibility; a human physiotherapist must bear direct responsibility.",
   "Full autonomy could let patients mistreat robots, damaging patients' own moral development.",
   "Emotional attachment to robots amounts to deception for young ASD patients.",
   "Privacy sensitivity is an additional ethical concern.",
   "Nursing robots should remain auxiliary tools under physiotherapist supervision."
  ],
